# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# `install.sh` is why this file exists: git's Windows default (`core.autocrlf`)
# checks a shell script out with CRLF, and bash then reads the carriage return
# as part of the interpreter path and dies with
#
#     ./install.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#     $'\r': command not found
#
# The other sources are LF-native too (TypeScript, the ESM build script, the
# YAML patch), so one rule covers the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf
